<section class="philosophy grain" id="philosophy">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--light" data-reveal>The analog-first philosophy</p>

    <h2 class="statement" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 90ms">The app isn't the point.</h2>

    <div class="statement-body">
      <p class="lede--light" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 160ms">
        This system intentionally lives primarily inside a physical notebook. The website helps you
        understand the method, set up your monthly spread, and review the months behind you. But the daily
        act of tracking belongs away from a screen.
      </p>
      <p class="lede--light" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 220ms">
        Your notebook shouldn't measure your productivity. It should help you notice your life — the run you
        almost skipped, the conversation that changed your week, the idea you'd have otherwise lost.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="moment" data-reveal style="--reveal-delay: 260ms">
      <p class="moment-line">Close the app.</p>
      <p class="moment-line moment-line--italic">Open the notebook.</p>
    </div>

    <p class="philosophy-foot mono" data-reveal>Paper first · screen second</p>
  </div>
</section>

